mastery.question_text:
The arc shown has a length of $4$ cm. Find the radius of the circle it came from, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.6);
\coordinate (B) at (30:2.6);
\draw (O) -- (A);
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw[very thick] (A) arc[start angle=0,end angle=30,radius=2.6];
\node at (15:3.15) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\pic[draw,"$30^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.6cm,angle eccentricity=3.1] {angle=A--O--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

